From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: respect local_out skb ownership on SOE completion

After local_out() is called, an skb is retained by the caller only when
the callback returns 1. Netfilter DROP consumes it and QUEUE/STOLEN may
retain it asynchronously; L3-master output handlers can also consume it.
Do not free it a second time when the callback returns another value.
Release the SOE context independently and continue dst_output only for 1,
matching the native IP/XFRM output contract.

Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5.6-sol
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_soe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_soe.c
@@ -1177,18 +1177,13 @@
 	net = dev_net(dst->dev);
 	nf_reset_ct(skb);
 	err = skb_dst(skb)->ops->local_out(net, NULL, skb);
-	if (unlikely(err != 1))
-		goto drop_skb;
 	kfree(ctx);
-	dst_output(net, NULL, skb);
+	/* A non-1 return means local_out already consumed or queued the skb. */
+	if (likely(err == 1))
+		dst_output(net, NULL, skb);
 
 	return true;
 
-drop_skb:
-	kfree(ctx);
-	kfree_skb(skb);
-	return true;
-
 drop:
 	dst_release(dst);
 	kfree(ctx);
